# MARKDOWN — prettier does not format it, by request from tosijs.
#
# It buys nothing here and it rewrites authored prose. `proseWrap` is already `preserve`,
# so the only things prettier changes in a .md file are: escaping literal characters
# (`a * literal` becomes `a \* literal`), padding table cells to align, and rewriting `*`
# bullets as `-`. None of that is a formatting decision anyone needs made for them, and the
# first one edits the CONTENT of a document rather than its layout.
#
# That matters more here than in most repos because **markdown is the product**: `src/docs/`
# is the doc corpus, and it is published as a site, an ePub and `llms.txt`. An author's
# deliberate character is not ours to normalise.
#
# Measured before doing this, and worth recording because it qualifies the case: the
# escaping is IDEMPOTENT (three further passes changed nothing) and renders identically
# through `renderDocMarkdown`, so this is churn and unwanted authority over prose — not the
# progressive corruption it is easy to assume. The reason to stop is that it has no upside,
# not that it is destroying files.
#
# The `*.md` override in .prettierrc.json (embeddedLanguageFormatting: off) is now redundant
# but harmless; it stays as the record of an earlier round of the same problem.
*.md
